# TARGET ARCHITECTURE: aarch64 (ARM64) | v0.16.3 | aws/ubuntu2604
# ARM64-specific syscall mapping; reconcile against this product/version ARM64 STIG or approved baseline.
# Enterprise Linux Audit v0.16.3  |  [aws/ubuntu2604]
# Tier: tier-1-baseline
# Purpose: MAC administrative policy changes and enforcement context
# Source/authority: DISA applicable product STIG/SRG as applicable; vendor SELinux/AppArmor docs
# Architecture: aarch64 (b64 only). No x86/compat b32 syscall rules.
# Release state: engineering candidate; NOT independently certified STIG compliant.


# Ubuntu 26.04 LTS (Resolute Raccoon), AppArmor 5.x.
# Source: Canonical 26.04 release/security documentation; OS profile derived from Ubuntu 24.04.
# DISA Ubuntu 26.04 STIG not verified as published as of 2026-11-07.
# This is an enterprise engineering baseline, NOT a validated 26.04 STIG rule mapping.
# AppArmor policies; AppArmor denials are logged through audit/journal/syslog as configured.
-a always,exit -F arch=b64 -F dir=/etc/apparmor.d -F perm=wa -k t1_apparmor_policy
# Ubuntu 26.04 package manifest: apparmor_parser is /usr/sbin/apparmor_parser (amd64 and arm64).
# Source: https://packages.ubuntu.com/resolute/amd64/apparmor/filelist
# Ubuntu 26.04 engineering baseline: AppArmor profile-load activity is required by enterprise policy.
# Verify parser executable location on the image; adapt the path if needed before deployment.
-a always,exit -F path=/usr/sbin/apparmor_parser -F perm=x -F auid>=1000 -F auid!=unset -k t1_apparmor_parser
